# How to cite Raphael. GitHub shows this as "Cite this repository", and
# Zenodo uses it for the DOI record of each release. Add yourself under
# `authors` when you contribute. `version` and `date-released` are updated
# by `release_tools.py prepare`.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Raphael, please cite the version you used (each release has its
  own DOI on Zenodo).
type: software
title: "Raphael: shared core for neural data processing and analysis"
abstract: >-
  Raphael turns raw neural recordings (Neuropixels, two-photon imaging, fibre
  photometry) into processed, publishable per-session files, and provides
  the analysis tools that the Mikulovic and Hangya labs' projects share.
authors:
  - given-names: Harry
    family-names: Clark
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/CogEmLab/Raphael"
keywords:
  - neuroscience
  - electrophysiology
  - spike sorting
  - calcium imaging
  - fiber photometry
  - NWB
version: 0.4.0
date-released: "2026-11-24"
